    (0, None, '\'Louis, are you still working in the kitchen?\' "Vsyo eshchyo", "still", is made from "vsyo", "everything", and "eshchyo", "yet". Max says "ty", so they are friends by now. "Rabotaesh" is "you work".'),
    (1, None, '\'Yes, I am making delicate chocolate cream.\' "Nezhny" means "tender" or "delicate", and Russians use it for cream and for people. "Shokoladny" is "chocolate" turned into a describing word, "chocolatey".'),
